rced it in Greece and  to the extent that restructuring or debt  write-offs you know our necessity in the  next few weeks which will be hard to  agree upon with all the EU members you  know it's a German lead decision you  know they suggested it's in the Greek  hands but I think it's in the German  hints and to the extent that the Germans  are unwilling to come off of their  position and to extend their marginal  line I think a grexit is a seventy to  eighty percent probability bill it's  amazing how distance can provide clarity  to a situation like this we thank you so  much that is Bill Gross a Janus Capital  manager of the Janus global  unconstrained bond fund
 

